1
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:27,920
NEW RACING KING

1.1
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:35,620
How fast.

2
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,080
Hello everyone.

3
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:45,540
Welcome to the Racing Life Remote Control Car Racing Championship.

4
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:47,520
Greetings to all of you.

5
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:51,700
Today, two racers will compete in the championship.

6
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:55,340
One is Liam, who has vast racing experience.

7
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:00,360
The other is Elvin, the youngest racer with a promising future.

8
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:04,540
We'll see who will be this year's racing king.

9
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:08,440
Our race will begin in half an hour, dear viewers.

10
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:10,240
We'll watch and see together.

11
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:17,000
Dad, you must definitely win this year's national championship.

12
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,200
Carson, the result is not important at all.

13
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:23,020
In fact, your father is very happy because he is going to race against Elvin.

14
00:02:23,020 --> 00:02:23,340
happy.

15
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:26,900
Elvin is a serious and intelligent racer.

16
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:29,400
Although his style seems a bit scattered,

17
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:33,500
his kamikaze move has enabled him to beat many competitors.

18
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:37,020
And more importantly...

19
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:39,700
Or are you going to say his hands-free Speed Stream ability?

20
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:44,780
Yes, until now, no one has been able to defeat that move of his.

21
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:45,200
defeat.

22
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:48,900
If I can't give it my all, I may never be able to beat him.

23
00:02:54,750 --> 00:02:56,890
what do you want from me?

24
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:04,190
Get out of my way, leave my car alone.

25
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:07,370
If you don't admit defeat, I won't let go.

26
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:08,390
No!

27
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:21,370
Turmoil!

28
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:30,590
I won the braking contest we did.

29
00:03:30,850 --> 00:03:32,310
Why should I accept defeat?

30
00:03:32,470 --> 00:03:35,150
Because if you don't, we'll wreck your racing car.

31
00:03:35,330 --> 00:03:37,910
No, my grandmother gave me this car.

32
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:38,810
So what?

33
00:03:39,350 --> 00:03:41,950
Look, your car has turned into a total wreck.

34
00:03:42,190 --> 00:03:43,850
Why not give up on it?

35
00:03:44,470 --> 00:03:45,450
Push harder, guys.

36
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:55,730
No way.

37
00:03:55,890 --> 00:03:58,970
Guys, how about we throw his car off the bridge?

38
00:03:59,570 --> 00:03:59,870
Stop!

39
00:04:10,790 --> 00:04:13,230
This guy is also a racer.

40
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:16,670
How can you treat another racer's cars like this?

41
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:17,390
treat?

42
00:04:18,269 --> 00:04:20,829
This is none of your business, you understand me?

43
00:04:20,829 --> 00:04:20,950
me?

44
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:32,720
You two, stop him.

45
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:34,680
I'll deal with this one.

46
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:35,760
Alright, alright.

47
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,780
Come here.

48
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,300
No way.

49
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:17,550
He's going to help him.

50
00:05:17,850 --> 00:05:18,890
Let's make them crash into each other.

51
00:05:19,070 --> 00:05:21,250
No, if I don't brake, it'll be too late.

52
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:25,790
Speed Stream!

53
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,620
It disappeared.

54
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:40,940
Where did that car go?

55
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,880
This is impossible.

56
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,760
He used Speed Stream.

57
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:46,800
Or is he...

58
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,340
Elvin, the Racing King!

59
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:54,940
My car!

60
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:04,590
Get away, get away quickly!

61
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:07,330
Are you okay, big brother?

62
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,210
I'm fine.

63
00:06:11,050 --> 00:06:12,130
Here's your car.

64
00:06:12,550 --> 00:06:14,430
Brother, you hurt your hand.

65
00:06:17,070 --> 00:06:18,130
No problem.

66
00:06:18,550 --> 00:06:20,710
A car is a racer's closest friend.

67
00:06:21,670 --> 00:06:25,110
No matter what, we must do everything to protect it.

68
00:06:25,110 --> 00:06:25,730
everything.

69
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:30,190
I hope you become an excellent racer in the future.

70
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,720
Let it begin now.

71
00:06:46,880 --> 00:06:47,620
Where are they?

72
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,260
What's going on?

73
00:06:57,480 --> 00:06:58,760
How much longer will we wait?

74
00:06:58,960 --> 00:06:59,500
Come on.

75
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:02,320
Hello everyone!

76
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:03,960
Sorry for the delay.

77
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:07,440
The tournament committee has decided to disqualify Elvin.

78
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:11,300
Because Elvin could not take his place at the designated time.

79
00:07:11,780 --> 00:07:15,620
Due to this situation, the winner of the race is automatically Liam!

80
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:34,020
Three years later.

81
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:41,360
Dad!

82
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,500
Yes, tell me Carson.

83
00:07:43,940 --> 00:07:45,300
Is my new car ready?

84
00:07:46,600 --> 00:07:48,960
This is my first year in the world racing championship.

85
00:07:49,100 --> 00:07:50,520
I need to practice immediately.

86
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:53,700
My goal is definitely to win the world championship.

87
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:56,500
It's finally finished.

88
00:08:04,610 --> 00:08:07,010
Here, I have my new car.

89
00:08:08,110 --> 00:08:09,910
The car's name is Storm Blade.

90
00:08:09,910 --> 00:08:13,130
It's manufactured entirely according to the characteristics of these races.

91
00:08:13,510 --> 00:08:15,650
It has everything needed for control.

92
00:08:15,850 --> 00:08:18,570
Its performance is extremely balanced and satisfying.

93
00:08:19,030 --> 00:08:22,230
I'm sure that with this vehicle, you'll be able to achieve many successes in the world championship.

94
00:08:22,230 --> 00:08:23,130
successes.

95
00:08:24,630 --> 00:08:27,590
Dad, do you think I have a chance to beat Elvin with this car?

96
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:28,570
chance?

97
00:08:28,970 --> 00:08:31,770
Elvin hasn't been seen around since that day.

98
00:08:31,970 --> 00:08:34,190
Since his disappearance three years ago, no one has seen him.

99
00:08:34,190 --> 00:08:35,049
seen him.

100
00:08:35,770 --> 00:08:37,669
I received the trophy in that championship.

101
00:08:37,669 --> 00:08:40,809
But in this racing world, he will always remain an invincible speed legend.

102
00:08:40,809 --> 00:08:42,570
legend.

103
00:08:43,210 --> 00:08:45,000
I haven't told anyone else, but...

104
00:08:45,570 --> 00:08:49,110
...being able to race against him in front of all the spectators was really something I wanted.

105
00:08:49,110 --> 00:08:49,430
wanted.

106
00:08:50,450 --> 00:08:53,090
Dad, is that why you withdrew from racing after that incident?

107
00:08:53,090 --> 00:08:54,450
incident?

108
00:08:54,590 --> 00:08:56,810
No, I got too old to race.

109
00:08:58,190 --> 00:09:00,570
In recent years, you've won all the trophies, son.

110
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,660
Come on, let's go try out your car, okay?

112
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:25,150
I've never seen such a beautiful performance.

113
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:26,450
Hey, this is Carson.

114
00:09:26,830 --> 00:09:28,990
The kid who won the last two national races.

115
00:09:29,410 --> 00:09:30,750
I watched his races.

116
00:09:30,990 --> 00:09:31,770
He's very tough.

117
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:34,330
It's said he hasn't lost a game.

118
00:09:34,710 --> 00:09:37,430
So far, no one has been able to break his record.

119
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:38,990
Great.

120
00:09:39,650 --> 00:09:40,690
Ready, aren't you?

121
00:09:46,810 --> 00:09:47,490
Start.

122
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:06,550
My new car is really awesome.

123
00:10:06,770 --> 00:10:07,830
Its takeoff is very fast.

124
00:10:07,990 --> 00:10:10,210
Also, its features are completely suited to me.

125
00:10:10,350 --> 00:10:12,550
This car has really turned out exactly as I dreamed.

126
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:12,970
dreamed.

127
00:10:16,730 --> 00:10:20,030
Dad, does the car have any other features besides providing better control?

128
00:10:20,030 --> 00:10:21,030
control?

129
00:10:22,010 --> 00:10:24,030
Press the left forward button and see.

130
00:10:29,490 --> 00:10:30,890
How is this?

131
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:33,030
This is a new trick.

132
00:10:33,270 --> 00:10:35,170
It's called Continuous Variable Transmission.

133
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:37,650
The remote control has different gears.

134
00:10:38,090 --> 00:10:41,150
When you select a gear, the car starts accelerating the moment it selects the gear.

135
00:10:41,150 --> 00:10:41,630
gear.

136
00:10:41,830 --> 00:10:44,250
Without you needing to watch the gear order.

137
00:10:45,230 --> 00:10:46,050
Wow.

138
00:10:47,770 --> 00:10:48,930
Storm Blade.

139
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:23,500
1-35-07

140
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:24,040
this means I beat my previous record.

141
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:24,980
That's it.

142
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:29,380
Carson, even though you improved your score, this will be your first appearance in the international arena.

143
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:31,000
arena.

144
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:32,980
You must work much harder.

145
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:34,500
Okay, dad.

146
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:35,560
Great, great.

147
00:11:36,880 --> 00:11:39,700
Now I saw someone using Speed Stream on the street.

148
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:42,980
So who is it?

149
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:46,180
They say he's one of the best racers in this community.

150
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:46,740
best.

151
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,080
The best?

152
00:11:48,380 --> 00:11:49,540
Speed Stream, huh.

153
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:50,760
Elvin.

153.1
00:12:06,540 --> 00:12:07,760
Be careful, Isaac!

154
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:12,080
Wake up guys, you're losing.

155
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:27,040
Are you the racer who uses Speed Stream?

156
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,500
Or do you also know Elvin?

157
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:32,260
Who taught you to use Speed Stream?

158
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,500
What's it to you?

159
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:34,840
And why should I tell you?

160
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,500
I know this kid.

161
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:45,840
Isn't this kid Carson, the winner of two national races?

162
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:46,380
right?

163
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:49,000
So how about racing against me?

164
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:51,920
Why would I race you?

165
00:12:52,160 --> 00:12:53,020
Don't be a coward.

166
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:54,840
Or are you afraid of me?

168
00:13:11,410 --> 00:13:13,370
Three-two-one go!

169
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:32,400
Very fast.

170
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,440
How does he do that?

171
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:35,980
I must definitely learn his secret.

172
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:38,280
Isaac starts in third gear.

173
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,720
That's why you've been lagging behind from the beginning.

174
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:44,040
Third gear?

175
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:46,660
If Isaac starts in first gear...

176
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:49,380
...he knows he'll fall behind right at the start...

177
00:13:49,380 --> 00:13:51,180
...and lose the race from the very beginning.

178
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:55,620
That's why he only uses third gear to accelerate.

179
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:57,520
Now I understand.

180
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,560
But doing that damages his car greatly.

181
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:02,860
Look at my new car.

182
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:04,960
I'm sure I'll catch up to his soon.

183
00:14:19,010 --> 00:14:21,770
Put aside those cool racer attitudes.

184
00:14:21,770 --> 00:14:24,310
I've been racing on these roads since I was little.

185
00:14:24,690 --> 00:14:26,130
Beating me won't be easy at all.

186
00:14:32,810 --> 00:14:35,380
My racing car is my father's latest invention.

187
00:14:35,940 --> 00:14:38,060
Do you think it'll lose to your antique?

188
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:40,000
Storm Blade now!

189
00:15:00,060 --> 00:15:02,540
Who is that kid challenging Isaac?

190
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:06,940
Carson, the kid who won two national racing championships.

191
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:11,460
He asked Isaac who taught him the Speed Stream he uses.

192
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:11,940
Stream.

193
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,800
But Isaac didn't tell him.

194
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:16,220
So Carson challenged him to a race.

195
00:15:22,490 --> 00:15:23,530
What's going on?

196
00:15:26,310 --> 00:15:27,070
How?

197
00:15:29,830 --> 00:15:32,130
Is there a problem with this road?

198
00:15:33,230 --> 00:15:36,530
This road is very different from other racing roads.

199
00:15:36,910 --> 00:15:37,930
Its surface is not smooth.

200
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:40,230
Therefore, it's a very challenging road for both the car and...

201
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:42,770
...the racer.

202
00:15:43,350 --> 00:15:45,270
Don't think that a national champion like you...

203
00:15:45,770 --> 00:15:48,070
...even with the best car on these roads...

204
00:15:48,070 --> 00:15:50,150
...has a guaranteed win.

205
00:15:50,370 --> 00:15:51,170
I see.

206
00:16:18,870 --> 00:16:21,290
How could he turn so fast from such a tight angle?

207
00:16:21,290 --> 00:16:22,130
angle?

208
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:28,650
And so confidently.

209
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:31,710
For that, the racer must be able to control his car very well...

210
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:32,990
...well.

211
00:16:33,490 --> 00:16:34,890
This kid is a good opponent for me.

212
00:16:35,190 --> 00:16:36,970
But I have no intention of losing.

213
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:50,020
One last curve remains.

214
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,360
If I can enter this curve ahead...

215
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,280
...I'll definitely be the winner of the race.

216
00:16:54,940 --> 00:16:55,880
Storm Blade!

217
00:17:12,510 --> 00:17:13,930
He thinks he'll enter the curve before me.

218
00:17:14,050 --> 00:17:15,390
Speed Stream!

219
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:35,120
How?

220
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:37,560
But this...

221
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:42,900
Be careful, Isaac!

222
00:18:11,260 --> 00:18:13,600
Sorry, but I didn't do it on purpose.

223
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:17,580
This car was my closest friend.

224
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:21,220
But you smashed it to pieces.

225
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,660
I will never forgive you.

226
00:18:28,980 --> 00:18:29,820
Wait.

227
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:31,880
You wrecked the kid's car.

228
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:32,860
What did you expect?

229
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:35,900
We don't want you here.

230
00:18:36,460 --> 00:18:37,060
Get out of here.

231
00:18:37,800 --> 00:18:38,960
That's terrible.

232
00:18:39,280 --> 00:18:40,340
Yes, I agree.

233
00:18:53,650 --> 00:18:55,510
The car is in very bad shape, Mina.

234
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:58,050
Do you think we can restore it to its former state?

235
00:18:58,390 --> 00:19:01,370
Isaac, these parts of the car are already outdated.

236
00:19:01,370 --> 00:19:03,370
Since it has undergone many modifications...

237
00:19:04,430 --> 00:19:07,010
...finding most parts will be quite difficult for us.

238
00:19:07,010 --> 00:19:07,490
difficult.

239
00:19:08,210 --> 00:19:09,810
Mina, please.

240
00:19:10,010 --> 00:19:11,870
You have to help him.

241
00:19:11,970 --> 00:19:12,430
Please!

242
00:19:13,170 --> 00:19:14,170
Don't worry.

243
00:19:15,050 --> 00:19:16,870
I'll gladly help you.

244
00:19:17,450 --> 00:19:19,070
You can go home now, Isaac.

245
00:19:19,830 --> 00:19:20,570
Thanks, Mina.

246
00:19:20,890 --> 00:19:21,390
Goodbye.

247
00:19:21,770 --> 00:19:22,610
See you tomorrow.

248
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:32,990
Alright.

249
00:19:33,650 --> 00:19:36,270
Now let's see where I'll find these parts.

250
00:19:36,650 --> 00:19:37,070
Huh?

251
00:19:41,790 --> 00:19:42,890
Come quickly!

252
00:19:43,070 --> 00:19:43,810
The thief is here!

253
00:19:48,470 --> 00:19:48,810
Dad!

254
00:19:49,650 --> 00:19:50,530
I'm not a thief.

255
00:19:52,770 --> 00:19:54,090
Tell me, Mina.

256
00:19:54,250 --> 00:19:56,930
Why are you up at this hour and what are you doing here?

257
00:19:58,270 --> 00:20:00,970
I want to find a new car for Isaac.

258
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:02,290
What happened?

259
00:20:02,690 --> 00:20:04,010
Did something happen to his car?

260
00:20:04,010 --> 00:20:06,710
Today, a kid came to race with Isaac.

261
00:20:06,930 --> 00:20:09,770
Before the last curve, he bumped into Isaac's car to get ahead...

262
00:20:09,770 --> 00:20:10,970
...and sent him off the track.

263
00:20:10,970 --> 00:20:12,150
track.

264
00:20:12,410 --> 00:20:14,650
During the spin, his car shattered to pieces.

265
00:20:14,850 --> 00:20:16,450
Isaac is a talented racer.

266
00:20:16,890 --> 00:20:19,570
Who would have the courage to challenge him like that?

267
00:20:19,570 --> 00:20:20,190
that?

268
00:20:20,630 --> 00:20:23,010
Supposedly, the kid was a winner of two national races.

269
00:20:23,730 --> 00:20:25,390
So what?

270
00:20:25,590 --> 00:20:28,970
Yeah, I understand, but Isaac's car was outdated.

271
00:20:28,970 --> 00:20:33,370
In fact, cars of the same model as his have even started to go out of circulation.

272
00:20:33,370 --> 00:20:35,930
circulation.

273
00:20:36,450 --> 00:20:39,890
So that's the main reason I couldn't find suitable parts for his car.

274
00:20:39,890 --> 00:20:40,810
car.

275
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:43,300
Dad, you are a racing car collector.

276
00:20:44,090 --> 00:20:46,080
You definitely have lots of parts.

277
00:20:46,970 --> 00:20:49,060
If I can't repair Isaac's car...

278
